{"path":"ranges/join_view/begin","title":"std::ranges::join_view<V>::begin","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::join_view&lt;V&gt;::</span>begin","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/join_view/begin","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"Returns an iterator to the first element of the join_view. Given base_ is the underlying view,","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/input_range\"><span class=\"kw2920\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">input_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_reference\"><span class=\"kw488\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_reference_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_reference_t\"><span class=\"kw2913\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns an <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_view/iterator\">iterator</a> to the first element of the <code>join_view</code>. Given <code><i>base_</i></code> is the underlying view,\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Equivalent to\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw2\">true</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*simple-view*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is satisfied and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_reference_t\"><span class=\"kw2913\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> is reference type. Otherwise,\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw2\">false</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> <span class=\"coMULTI\">/*iterator*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw2\">true</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Iterator to the first element.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>When <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_reference_t\"><span class=\"kw2913\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> is not a reference type, that is, deferencing an iterator of <code>V</code> returns a prvalue temporary, the <code>join_view</code> is only an <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/input_range\"><code>input_range</code></a>, in which case only single-pass iteration is supported, and repeated calls to <code>begin()</code> may not give meaningful results.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/join_view/end\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>end</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an iterator or a sentinel to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::begin</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> returns an iterator to the beginning of a range<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(customization point object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/join_view","title":"std::ranges::views::join, std::ranges::join_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::join_view<V>::begin","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Returns an iterator to the first element of the join_view. Given base_ is the underlying view,"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Iterator to the first element."},{"label":"Notes","note":"When ranges::range_reference_t<V> is not a reference type, that is, deferencing an iterator of V returns a prvalue temporary, the join_view is only an…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"end","note":"returns an iterator or a sentinel to the end"},{"label":"ranges::begin","note":"returns an iterator to the beginning of a range"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":146,"codeBlockCount":0}
